<title>GERMANY: German May vehicle production down 5 pct - VDA.</title>
<headline>German May vehicle production down 5 pct - VDA.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The VDA German motor vehicle association published the following production figures for May compared to May 1996.</p>
<p>Total vehicles</p>
<p>   Production				 400,300  vs down 5 pct</p>
<p>   Exports				    232,200  vs down 2 pct</p>
<p>Cars, estates (station wagons)</p>
<p>    Production			     375,300  vs down 5 pct</p>
<p>    Exports				  215,900  vs down 2 pct</p>
<p>Trucks</p>
<p>    Production				25,000  vs up 10 pct</p>
<p>    Exports				   16,300  vs up 7 pct</p>
<p>Trucks to 6 tonnes</p>
<p>    Production				14,800  vs up 7 pct</p>
<p>    Exports				    9,600  vs down 1 pct</p>
<p>Trucks over 6 tonnes</p>
<p>    Production				10,200  vs up 16 pct</p>
<p>    Exports				    6,700  vs up 21 pct</p>
<p>The VDA also provided the following data for the year between January and May compared to the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>Total vehicles</p>
<p>    Production			    2,131,500 vs unchanged</p>
<p>    Exports				 1,276,800 vs up 5 pct</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
